    "long_instructions": "*This level follows a video that you may have watched with your class. If you missed the video, you can watch [here](https://youtu.be/Hjl6gbg9kmk).*\r\n\r\n# Add Text to the Body\r\n\r\nWhen you start any new project, it will automatically add `<!DOCTYPE>`, `<html>`, and `<body>` tags to your project. When you add content to your projects, you'll need to do it between the `<body>` and `</body>` tags because it should be part of the body of your webpage.\r\n\r\nAnother student, Sofia, has already started adding text to her webpage. She started to add paragraph tags so each sentence would appear on its own line, but hasn't finished.\r\n\r\n# Do This\r\n\r\n1) Finish adding `<p>` and `</p>` tags to Sofia's code so each sentence appears on a separate line.\r\n\r\n  **Note:** Web Lab 2 automatically adds a closing `</p>` tag as soon as you type `<p>` — but it lands immediately after the opening tag (`<p></p>Hello`), not after your text. You'll need to move the `</p>` (or delete it and retype it) so it ends up after the sentence, like `<p>Hello</p>`.\r\n2) Use the Inspector Tool to verify that each line has a paragraph tag.\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n::: details [🔎 **Show Me How** 🔍]\r\n![Adding p tags](https://images.code.org/a33dbd8814a9a8389f4d92e06b3089f6-image-1784847464265.png)\r\n:::\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n::: details [Help & Tips]\r\n[<i class=\"fa-solid fa-book\"></i> HTML Tags](https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/courses/csd-2024/guides/html-tags)\r\n:::",
